{UTF-8}
Potential Adopters= INTEG (
	-Adoption from Advertising-Adoption from Word of Mouth,
		10000)
	~	Persons
	~	Bass (1969) diffusion, written for SD Lab after Sterman (2000) Business Dynamics ch. 9.3: who has not adopted yet.
	|
Adopters= INTEG (
	Adoption from Advertising+Adoption from Word of Mouth-Discontinuation,
		0)
	~	Persons
	~	Who uses the product now.
	|
Adoption from Advertising=
	Advertising Effectiveness*Potential Adopters
	~	Persons/Month
	~	The innovation term p x P.
	|
Adoption from Word of Mouth=
	Contact Rate*Adoption Fraction*Potential Adopters*Adopters/Total Market
	~	Persons/Month
	~	The imitation term q x P x A / N.
	|
Discontinuation=
	Adopters/Product Life
	~	Persons/Month
	~	Adopters who stop using it (Bass with discontinuance).
	|
Advertising Effectiveness=
	0.01
	~	1/Month
	~	p
	|
Contact Rate=
	10
	~	Contacts/Person/Month
	~	
	|
Adoption Fraction=
	0.04
	~	Dmnl
	~	q = contact rate x adoption fraction = 0.4
	|
Total Market=
	10000
	~	Persons
	~	N, held constant
	|
Product Life=
	50
	~	Month
	~	
	|
********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|
FINAL TIME  = 60
	~	Month
	~		|
INITIAL TIME  = 0
	~	Month
	~		|
SAVEPER  = 
        TIME STEP
	~	Month
	~		|
TIME STEP  = 0.25
	~	Month
	~		|
